mod:addr_via_pointer_deep_prices_1;
// 2026-11-18 (landing 177d2c, row 1: DEF-644 root B at every depth). An address taken through a pointer names storage that pointer points at, and
// 177d2b9's row 3 rerooted it ONE level. Where a target is itself a place through a pointer (`r3 = @(<-r)` over `r = @((<-q0).inner)`; `sp =
// @(<-sp1)` over `sp1 = @(<-sp2)`), its root's chain is still a pointer's own, so a store landing two or more levels down went unrecorded: by the
// record, by the store's descents, on the two rootless roads, or through V's held arms at the last hop. A growth of what was stored then freed
// what the place read. The escape analysis now walks every place such an address reaches (`reroot_closure`: a worklist with a memo, a fold by
// full ref, a per-call stamp, bounded by the tree with a guard that fails closed), and the record, `rrti_path`'s and `rrti_chain`'s descents, the
// rootless destination, a storing callee's rootless pointer argument and V's last-hop arms all read it. A fix only adds records beside main's.
// THE PRICES (39), each running 67 on R3F (524cf77) and refused here, each beside its twins refused on R3F (TWINS, 35); its twins that run 67 on
// both are in tests/backend/programs/addr_via_pointer_deep_ok.npk. The prices: `rl_pp1_ok`, `rl_pp2_ok`, `kp_V_ok`, `kp_M_ok`, `s_ks_V_ok`,
// `s_ks_M_ok`, `a5_hpc_ok`, `a5_if_ok`, `a5_loop_ok`, `a5_rsg_ok`, `a5_view_ok`, `fu_self8_ok`, `fu_self40_ok`, `fu_self62_ok`, `fu_self63_ok`,
// `fu_self64_ok`, `fu_self65_ok`, `fu_self70_ok`, `fu_self130_ok`, `d_res2_ok`, `d_res3_ok`, `d_tern2_ok`, `pf_2`, `pf_3`, `pf_r1`, `pf_r2`,
// `pk_t2`, `pd2b_o`, `pd2c_o`, `pd3y_o`, `mt_un1_ok`, `mt_un2_ok`, `mt_un3_ok`, `mt_cu1_ok`, `mt_cu2_ok`, `mt_cu3_ok`, `mt_cp1_ok`, `mt_cp2_ok`,
// `mt_cp3_ok`. The twins: `rl_pp0_ok`, `rl_ppn_ok`, `rl_ppd_ok`, `kp_W_ok`, `s_ks_W_ok`, `a5_hpc_ok_pt`, `a5_if_ok_pt`, `a5_loop_ok_pt`,
// `a5_rsg_ok_pt`, `a5_view_ok_pt`, `fu_self8_ok_pt`, `fu_self40_ok_pt`, `fu_self62_ok_pt`, `fu_self63_ok_pt`, `fu_self64_ok_pt`,
// `fu_self65_ok_pt`, `fu_self70_ok_pt`, `fu_self130_ok_pt`, `d_res0_ok`, `d_tern0_ok`, `d_resd_ok`, `d_ternd_ok`, `d_res1_ok`, `d_tern1_ok`,
// `pf_n`, `pf_rd`, `pf_d`, `pf_1`, `pk_tn`, `pk_t1`, `pd1b_o`, `pd0b_o`, `pd3z_o`, `mt_un_pl_ok`, `mt_c_pl_ok`. All are at parity but piece (c)'s
// four, `kp_V_ok`, `kp_M_ok`, `s_ks_V_ok`, `s_ks_M_ok`: off parity by their zero-loop twins and by the D-286 twins that read on a fresh local, it
// is main's D-286 hold and main's loop record met through (c)'s true record, and takes DEF-694 (LOW; rulings l.16508 and l.16641). Six of them
// moved here from tests/backend/programs/addr_via_pointer_store_ok.npk.
// 2026-11-19 (landing 177d2d, row 2: row 1 of 177d2c held out, now rebased onto aefae6e as R1-4 with the cost fix, its price DEF-694; rulings l.19112 and l.19370):
// `pk2_ok`, `pk2c_ok` and `pk3_ok` join the prices from tests/backend/programs/addr_via_pointer_store_ok.npk, each refused here at BORROW-009 and at
// parity with `pk2_lc_ok` (l.19112 item 4). The other prices and twins stand as written, measured on main (aefae6e) and R1-4.
// 2026-11-19 (landing 177d2d, row 2: row 1 of 177d2c held out, now rebased onto aefae6e as R1-4 with the cost fix, its price DEF-694; rulings l.19112 and l.19370):
// R1c's prices file (74 units, 83 sites; 77 units with the three moved here) is split by whole units, at a group's head, into 2 files for the
// harness's 20 s limit on a rejection file (harness.py l.2156): whole, it compiled in 11.0 s on R1-4 and 9.8 s on main at load 7.2. This is part 1
// of 2: its units rl_pp1_ok to fu_self130_ok_pt. The list above is the whole file's.
error:E5;
// PRICES (rulings l.16403 item 4 (147's rootless road; zero-level, by-name and direct twins)): each runs 67 on R3F (524cf77) and is refused here; its twins refused on R3F follow, and its twins that run 67 on both are in the ok file.
